#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:5 ec3fb520b9aa4b91ae4ec8bb10f7ca0b
msgid "Stabilize Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:7 ab66d308d09948e295ce91931d2fa125
msgid ""
"Stabilize mode allows you to fly your vehicle manually, but self-levels the "
"roll and pitch axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:12 4ad7226b72d44f9e8b0cd536a2f16bd3
msgid ""
"If you're learning to fly, try :ref:`Alt Hold <altholdmode>` or :ref:`Loiter"
" <loiter-mode>` instead of Stabilize. You'll have fewer crashes if you don't"
" need to concentrate on too many controls at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:20 d1d0489a453b4547a5f5bf2f729aecd7
msgid ""
"While stabilize mode does not necessarily require GPS, switching to RTL in "
"case of emergency does. Make sure you do have a reliable position estimate "
"prior to arming, most commonly provided by 3D GPS fix with sufficient HDOP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:25 a33ab160fa974dfba78185a7c83d5013
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:27 7d1571dae2e34341afcda51532494630
msgid ""
"Pilot's roll and pitch input control the lean angle of the copter. When the "
"pilot releases the roll and pitch sticks the vehicle automatically levels "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:30 32afc80623af45209168606befcdfb01
msgid ""
"Pilot will need to regularly input roll and pitch commands to keep the "
"vehicle in place as it is pushed around by the wind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:32 373c45e43e3a4799b7672d8d6a2d5156
msgid ""
"Pilot's yaw input controls the rate of change of the heading.  When the "
"pilot releases the yaw stick the vehicle will maintain its current heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:35 09da8bdcd902481388aae9e25e6e34d7
msgid ""
"Pilot's throttle input controls the average motor speed meaning that "
"constant adjustment of the throttle is required to maintain altitude.  If "
"the pilot puts the throttle completely down the motors will go to their "
"minimum rate (MOT_SPIN_ARMED) and if the vehicle is flying it will lose "
"attitude control and tumble. However, this behavior can be changed by "
"enabling :ref:`airmode`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:41 86ede54e03264a3a9d70f9530e80e20a
msgid ""
"The throttle sent to the motors is automatically adjusted based on the tilt "
"angle of the vehicle (i.e. increased as the vehicle tilts over more) to "
"reduce the compensation the pilot must do as the vehicle's attitude changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:48 2901e30da5f54cbc9e1ab7cf21f11f9a
msgid ""
"Always switch into a manual mode such as stabilize if the autopilot fails to"
" control the vehicle. Maintaining control of your copter is your "
"responsibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:53 370686814e1140668c0127ab46b500be
msgid "AirMode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:55 a5a9ccbf58324289ae919050ed84ce4a
msgid ""
"Stabilize mode can be setup to provide full stabilization at idle throttle. "
"See :ref:`airmode`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:60 b35dc1e0c25d40d9a5a33cd9389716db
msgid "Tuning"
msgstr "调参"

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:62 3463fd6bf1b8461e9874be797ebbc285
msgid "See :ref:`common-tuning` for complete tuning topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:64 1c6e2921777f4ea883ba9caf5d954f08
msgid ""
"Using :ref:`AutoTune <autotune>` may allow you to automatically determine "
"the best Stabilize and Rate PID values. It is highly suggested running "
"AutoTune on your vehicle rather than manually adjusting PIDs. However, see "
":ref:`ac_rollpitchtuning` for roll and pitch manual tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:68 c118fc531a4e43ce8a1398e868df0382
msgid "Other important parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:69 2191d672696348b48b3a7fbd68704bd8
msgid ""
":ref:`ANGLE_MAX<ANGLE_MAX>` controls the maximum lean angle which by default"
" is 4500 (i.e. 45 degrees)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:71 9c0cdfc686e04052884c459721cc6d1e
msgid ""
"ANGLE_RATE_MAX controls the maximum requested rotation rate in the roll and "
"pitch axis which by default is 18000 (180deg/sec)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:73 8beb0003969f47a298bf462bee18b0c8
msgid ""
":ref:`ACRO_Y_RATE<ACRO_Y_RATE>` controls how quickly copter rotates based on"
" a pilot's yaw input.  The default of 4.5 commands a 200 deg/sec rate of "
"rotation when the yaw stick is held fully left or right.  Higher values will"
" make it rotate more quickly."
msgstr ""
